    {
      "id": "KA-C104-accusative-annu",
      "sequence": 4172,
      "title": "-ಅನ್ನು (-annu) — the person or particular thing an action reaches",
      "headword": "-ಅನ್ನು",
      "romanization": "-annu",
      "gloss": "the object ending: the person or particular thing an action reaches",
      "script": "kannada",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:c0753f4a979396c5",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Your first visible case ending was -ಗೆ: one piece on the end for one job. Say the Kannada for the police and for a shop. This lesson gives a second ending and one new job."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: -ಅನ್ನು marks the object",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪೊಲೀಸರನ್ನು ಕರೆಯಿರಿ polīsarannu kareyiri — please call the police."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The calling reaches ಪೊಲೀಸರು (polīsaru), “the police”. Kannada puts -ಅನ್ನು (-annu) on that object: ಪೊಲೀಸರು becomes ಪೊಲೀಸರನ್ನು. The final sound joins the ending, but the job stays visible."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With a person, the object ending is required. With a non-human thing, it often marks a particular thing already in view:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "the word",
                "as the object",
                "meaning"
              ],
              "columns": 3,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "the word: ಪೊಲೀಸರು polīsaru. as the object: ಪೊಲೀಸರನ್ನು polīsarannu. meaning: the police, as the people called.",
                "the word: ಅಂಗಡಿ aṅgaḍi. as the object: ಅಂಗಡಿಯನ್ನು aṅgaḍiyannu. meaning: the particular shop, as the thing acted on."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is the accusative, the direct-object case. Keep the practical question: who or what does the action reach? Put its marker on that word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two case endings, two jobs: -ಗೆ points to a receiver or experiencer; -ಅನ್ನು (-annu) marks the object an action reaches. Kannada keeps the jobs in separate pieces rather than hiding both inside one ending."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "polīsaru … polīsarannu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *polīsaru … polīsarannu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "aṅgaḍi … aṅgaḍiyannu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *aṅgaḍi … aṅgaḍiyannu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "polīsarannu kareyiri — please call the police",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
